{"toolCallId":"call_45dce71efaa34c13b15b6a4605fde62d","title":"Edit file","kind":"edit","content":[{"type":"diff","path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/wff82223311/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/tasks.md","oldText":"---\ntitle: \"Tasks: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\"\ndescription: \"Task Format: T### [P?] Description (file path)\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"completeness min percent tasks\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.2 -->\n# Tasks: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n## Task Notation\n\n| Prefix | Meaning |\n|--------|---------|\n| `[ ]` | Pending |\n| `[x]` | Completed |\n| `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n| `[B]` | Blocked |\n\n**Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path)`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n## Phase 1: Setup\n\n- [ ] T001 Read the argument loop, both output functions and the `--file` NOT FOUND branch, and record which variable holds the percentage each path reports (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`)\n- [ ] T002 Read the existing vitest file and confirm the `spawnSync` helper and temp-packet teardown it already provides (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/calculate-completeness-script.vitest.ts`)\n- [ ] T003 [P] Confirm the test command for the suite and run it once to capture the baseline of the two existing cases (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/calculate-completeness-script.vitest.ts`)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n## Phase 2: Implementation\n\n- [ ] T004 Add `MIN_PERCENT=\"\"` and `REPORTED_PERCENTAGE=100` to the globals block beside `VERBOSE` and `OVERALL_PERCENTAGE` (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`)\n- [ ] T005 Add the `--min-percent) MIN_PERCENT=\"${2:-}\"; shift 2 ;;` arm to the argument loop, reading the value as `${2:-}` so `set -u` cannot abort on a trailing flag (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`)\n- [ ] T006 Add `validate_min_percent()` and call it after parsing but before the folder is read; reject a non-integer or an out-of-range value with a stderr message naming the option and exit `1` (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`)\n- [ ] T007 Assign `REPORTED_PERCENTAGE` from `OVERALL_PERCENTAGE` in folder mode and from the sourced `percentage` in `--file` mode, and set it to `0` in the NOT FOUND branch, without changing a printed line (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`)\n- [ ] T008 Replace the closing `exit 0` with the gate: `exit 3` when `MIN_PERCENT` is set and `REPORTED_PERCENTAGE` is below it, otherwise `exit 0` (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`)\n- [ ] T009 Add the `--min-percent <N>` line to the help OPTIONS block and an example, and document status `3` in the trailing exit-code comment (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n## Phase 3: Verification\n\n- [ ] T010 Add cases for below/at/above the floor asserting statuses `3`, `0`, `0` against a packet with a deterministic percentage (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/calculate-completeness-script.vitest.ts`)\n- [ ] T011 Add cases asserting stdout is identical with and without the flag, in text mode and under `--json` (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/calculate-completeness-script.vitest.ts`)\n- [ ] T012 Add cases for a missing value, `abc`, `-1` and `101`, each asserting exit `1`, empty stdout and an option-naming stderr message (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/calculate-completeness-script.vitest.ts`)\n- [ ] T013 Add a `--file` case above the file's percentage and its `--json` counterpart, asserting the status survives with the payload intact (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/calculate-completeness-script.vitest.ts`)\n- [ ] T014 Run the vitest file and confirm the new cases and the two pre-existing cases all pass (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/calculate-completeness-script.vitest.ts`)\n- [ ] T015 Diff the report of a real packet with and without `--min-percent 50`, and confirm the help text names the option (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n## Completion Criteria\n\n- [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\n- [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n- [ ] Manual verification passed\n- [ ] `REQ-001` through `REQ-006` each have an executed check recorded against them\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n## Cross-References\n\n- **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n- **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n\n---\n","newText":"---\ntitle: \"Tasks: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\"\ndescription: \"Task Format: T### [P?] Description (file path)\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"completeness min percent tasks\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.2 -->\n# Tasks: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n## Task Notation\n\n| Prefix | Meaning |\n|--------|---------|\n| `[ ]` | Pending |\n| `[x]` | Completed |\n| `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n| `[B]` | Blocked |\n\n**Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path)`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n## Phase 1: Setup\n\n- [ ] T001 Read the argument loop, both output functions and the `--file` NOT FOUND branch, and record which variable holds the percentage each path reports (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`)\n- [ ] T002 Read the existing vitest file and confirm the `spawnSync` helper and temp-packet teardown it already provides (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/calculate-completeness-script.vitest.ts`)\n- [ ] T003 [P] Confirm the test command for the suite and run it once to capture the baseline of the two existing cases (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/calculate-completeness-script.vitest.ts`)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n## Phase 2: Implementation\n\n- [ ] T004 Add `MIN_PERCENT=\"\"` and `REPORTED_PERCENTAGE=100` to the globals block beside `VERBOSE` and `OVERALL_PERCENTAGE` (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`)\n- [ ] T005 Add the `--min-percent) MIN_PERCENT=\"${2:-}\"; shift 2 ;;` arm to the argument loop, reading the value as `${2:-}` so `set -u` cannot abort on a trailing flag (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`)\n- [ ] T006 Add `validate_min_percent()` and call it after parsing but before the folder is read; reject a non-integer or an out-of-range value with a stderr message naming the option and exit `1` (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`)\n- [ ] T007 Assign `REPORTED_PERCENTAGE` from `OVERALL_PERCENTAGE` in folder mode and from the sourced `percentage` in `--file` mode, and set it to `0` in the NOT FOUND branch, without changing a printed line (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`)\n- [ ] T008 Replace the closing `exit 0` with the gate: `exit 3` when `MIN_PERCENT` is set and `REPORTED_PERCENTAGE` is below it, otherwise `exit 0` (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`)\n- [ ] T009 Add the `--min-percent <N>` line to the help OPTIONS block and an example, and document status `3` in the trailing exit-code comment (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`)\n- [ ] T016 Implement `REQ-007`: add `min_percent_met` to the `--json` payload when `--min-percent` is set, comparing `REPORTED_PERCENTAGE` against the floor, without changing any other key (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n## Phase 3: Verification\n\n- [ ] T010 Add cases for below/at/above the floor asserting statuses `3`, `0`, `0` against a packet with a deterministic percentage (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/calculate-completeness-script.vitest.ts`)\n- [ ] T011 Add cases asserting stdout is identical with and without the flag, in text mode and under `--json` (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/calculate-completeness-script.vitest.ts`)\n- [ ] T012 Add cases for a missing value, `abc`, `-1` and `101`, each asserting exit `1`, empty stdout and an option-naming stderr message (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/calculate-completeness-script.vitest.ts`)\n- [ ] T013 Add a `--file` case above the file's percentage and its `--json` counterpart, asserting the status survives with the payload intact (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/calculate-completeness-script.vitest.ts`)\n- [ ] T014 Run the vitest file and confirm the new cases and the two pre-existing cases all pass (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/calculate-completeness-script.vitest.ts`)\n- [ ] T015 Diff the report of a real packet with and without `--min-percent 50`, and confirm the help text names the option (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n## Completion Criteria\n\n- [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\n- [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n- [ ] Manual verification passed\n- [ ] `REQ-001` through `REQ-006` each have an executed check recorded against them\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n## Cross-References\n\n- **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n- **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n\n---\n","_meta":{"cognition.ai/linesAdded":1,"cognition.ai/linesRemoved":0}}],"locations":[{"path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/wff82223311/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/tasks.md"}],"rawInput":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/wff82223311/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/tasks.md"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"edit"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_475f5a3d492a4a5cbfacdd32767075a0","title":"Edit file","kind":"edit","content":[{"type":"diff","path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/wff82223311/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/spec.md","oldText":"---\ntitle: \"Feature Specification: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\"\ndescription: \"calculate-completeness.sh reports a completion percentage but always exits 0, so callers cannot gate on it. A --min-percent <N> option makes the script fail the process when completion falls below a caller-chosen floor, without changing a byte of its report.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"completeness min percent\"\n  - \"add a min percent option to calculate completeness\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: spec-core | v2.2 -->\n# Feature Specification: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 1 -->\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:metadata -->\n## 1. METADATA\n\n| Field | Value |\n|-------|-------|\n| **Level** | 1 |\n| **Priority** | P1 |\n| **Status** | Draft |\n| **Created** | 2026-10-26 |\n| **Branch** | `scaffold/001-completeness-min-percent` |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:metadata -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:problem -->\n## 2. PROBLEM & PURPOSE\n\n### Problem Statement\n`calculate-completeness.sh` computes an `Overall Completion` percentage and then unconditionally runs `exit 0`. Any caller that wants to refuse a packet below a quality floor has to scrape the number out of the human-readable report or the `--json` payload and compare it itself, so the check is reimplemented per caller and drifts from the script's own arithmetic. The script already owns the percentage; it should be able to own the comparison too.\n\n### Purpose\nAdd a `--min-percent <N>` option so the script's exit status answers \"is this packet at or above the floor?\" while its printed report stays exactly as it is today.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:problem -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:scope -->\n## 3. SCOPE\n\n### In Scope\n- A `--min-percent <N>` option on `calculate-completeness.sh`, accepted anywhere in the argument list alongside the existing options.\n- A threshold gate evaluated after the report is written: exit `3` when the reported completion is below `N`, exit `0` when it is at or above `N`.\n- Input validation for `N`: a base-10 integer from `0` to `100`, with a missing value reported as a usage error.\n- Help text and the script's trailing exit-code comment updated to describe the new option and status.\n\n### Out of Scope\n- Any change to how completion is calculated, which files are scanned, or which placeholders are counted - the feature gates the existing number, it does not redefine it.\n- Any change to the text or JSON report - the report is the contract callers already parse.\n- Changes to `validate.sh`, `check-completion.sh`, or any other script that might later pass the flag - this packet adds the capability, not its adoption.\n- Renumbering the repository-wide spec-script exit-code taxonomy - exit `3` is used here because the feature requires it, and the collision is recorded as a risk rather than resolved here.\n\n### Files to Change\n\n| File Path | Change Type | Description |\n|-----------|-------------|-------------|\n| `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh` | Modify | Add the option, its validation, the shared reported-percentage value, the post-output exit gate, and the help/exit-code text |\n| `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/calculate-completeness-script.vitest.ts` | Modify | Cover below/at/above threshold, unchanged report, invalid input, and the `--json` and `--file` paths |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:scope -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:requirements -->\n## 4. REQUIREMENTS\n\n### P0 - Blockers (MUST complete)\n\n| ID | Requirement | Acceptance Criteria |\n|----|-------------|---------------------|\n| REQ-001 | `calculate-completeness.sh` accepts `--min-percent <N>` as an option in any position among the existing options, and leaves the gate inactive when the option is absent. | `bash calculate-completeness.sh --min-percent 50 specs/001-x` parses without a usage error; the same folder without the flag still exits `0` as it does today. |\n| REQ-002 | With `--min-percent <N>`, the script exits `3` when the reported completion percentage is strictly below `N`, and exits `0` when it is at or above `N`. | A packet measured at 40% exits `3` under `--min-percent 50`, exits `0` under `--min-percent 40`, and exits `0` under `--min-percent 30`. |\n| REQ-003 | The report is unchanged: text and `--json` output are byte-identical with and without `--min-percent`. | `diff` of the stdout of the two invocations on the same packet is empty, for both the default and `--json` output modes. |\n\n### P1 - Required (complete OR user-approved deferral)\n\n| ID | Requirement | Acceptance Criteria |\n|----|-------------|---------------------|\n| REQ-004 | A missing, non-integer, or out-of-range `N` is rejected with a message on stderr and exit `1`, and no report is printed. | `--min-percent`, `--min-percent abc`, `--min-percent -1` and `--min-percent 101` each exit `1` with an error naming the option; stdout stays empty. |\n| REQ-005 | The threshold applies to the percentage the run actually reports: `OVERALL_PERCENTAGE` in folder mode and the single file's completion in `--file` mode, with the gate still active under `--json`. | A `--file` run at 0% under `--min-percent 1` exits `3`; the same run under `--json` preserves both the payload and the status. |\n| REQ-006 | `--help` lists `--min-percent <N>` in its OPTIONS block, and the script's trailing exit-code comment documents exit `3`. | `--help` output contains the new option line; the comment block at the end of the file names status `3` and its meaning. |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:requirements -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n## 5. SUCCESS CRITERIA\n\n- **SC-001**: The three threshold outcomes are observable as distinct exit statuses, verified by script invocation rather than by reading the source.\n- **SC-002**: A byte-for-byte comparison of the report with and without the flag is empty in both output modes.\n- **SC-003**: The existing vitest cases in `calculate-completeness-script.vitest.ts` still pass unchanged, and the new cases cover every row of REQ-001 through REQ-006.\n\n**Acceptance scenarios**\n\n- **Given** a packet whose `Overall Completion` is 40%, **When** the script runs with `--min-percent 50`, **Then** it prints the same report it prints without the flag and exits `3`.\n- **Given** the same packet, **When** the script runs with `--min-percent 40`, **Then** it prints that report and exits `0`, because the floor is inclusive.\n- **Given** any packet, **When** the script runs with no `--min-percent`, **Then** it exits `0` exactly as it did before the change.\n- **Given** a `--min-percent` value that is not an integer from `0` to `100`, **When** the script runs, **Then** it writes a usage error to stderr, prints no report, and exits `1`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:risks -->\n## 6. RISKS & DEPENDENCIES\n\n| Type | Item | Impact | Mitigation |\n|------|------|--------|------------|\n| Dependency | `bc`, plus the `find`/`grep`/`wc` coreutils the script already requires | None beyond today's baseline; the gate adds no new binary | Reuse the existing `command -v bc` guard; no new dependency is introduced |\n| Dependency | `set -euo pipefail` with `trap ... EXIT` | An unset or empty `N` would abort on `$2` under `set -u` with an unhelpful message, and the trap must still clean the temp directory on the new exit path | Read the value as `${2:-}` before use, and exit only after the report is written so the trap runs normally |\n| Risk | Exit `3` collides with the repository's spec-script taxonomy, where `3` means a system error | Medium - a caller that branches on `3` cannot distinguish \"below floor\" from \"I/O failure\" | The feature fixes the status at `3`; the collision is documented in the script's exit-code comment so the meaning stays discoverable |\n| Risk | The gate must not perturb the report | Medium - a stray `echo` or a reordered statement breaks callers that diff output | Gate after both output functions return, and assert byte equality in the test suite |\n| Risk | A caller runs the script under `set -e` and now sees a non-zero status it did not handle | Low - only callers that opt in pass the flag | Opt-in only: with no flag, the status is unchanged |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:risks -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:questions -->\n## 7. OPEN QUESTIONS\n\nNone. The feature statement fixes the option name, its argument, and the two statuses; the remaining choices (validation bounds, the value compared in `--file` mode) are recorded as requirements rather than left open.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:questions -->\n\n---\n","newText":"---\ntitle: \"Feature Specification: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\"\ndescription: \"calculate-completeness.sh reports a completion percentage but always exits 0, so callers cannot gate on it. A --min-percent <N> option makes the script fail the process when completion falls below a caller-chosen floor, without changing a byte of its report.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"completeness min percent\"\n  - \"add a min percent option to calculate completeness\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: spec-core | v2.2 -->\n# Feature Specification: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 1 -->\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:metadata -->\n## 1. METADATA\n\n| Field | Value |\n|-------|-------|\n| **Level** | 1 |\n| **Priority** | P1 |\n| **Status** | Draft |\n| **Created** | 2026-10-26 |\n| **Branch** | `scaffold/001-completeness-min-percent` |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:metadata -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:problem -->\n## 2. PROBLEM & PURPOSE\n\n### Problem Statement\n`calculate-completeness.sh` computes an `Overall Completion` percentage and then unconditionally runs `exit 0`. Any caller that wants to refuse a packet below a quality floor has to scrape the number out of the human-readable report or the `--json` payload and compare it itself, so the check is reimplemented per caller and drifts from the script's own arithmetic. The script already owns the percentage; it should be able to own the comparison too.\n\n### Purpose\nAdd a `--min-percent <N>` option so the script's exit status answers \"is this packet at or above the floor?\" while its printed report stays exactly as it is today.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:problem -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:scope -->\n## 3. SCOPE\n\n### In Scope\n- A `--min-percent <N>` option on `calculate-completeness.sh`, accepted anywhere in the argument list alongside the existing options.\n- A threshold gate evaluated after the report is written: exit `3` when the reported completion is below `N`, exit `0` when it is at or above `N`.\n- Input validation for `N`: a base-10 integer from `0` to `100`, with a missing value reported as a usage error.\n- Help text and the script's trailing exit-code comment updated to describe the new option and status.\n\n### Out of Scope\n- Any change to how completion is calculated, which files are scanned, or which placeholders are counted - the feature gates the existing number, it does not redefine it.\n- Any change to the text or JSON report - the report is the contract callers already parse.\n- Changes to `validate.sh`, `check-completion.sh`, or any other script that might later pass the flag - this packet adds the capability, not its adoption.\n- Renumbering the repository-wide spec-script exit-code taxonomy - exit `3` is used here because the feature requires it, and the collision is recorded as a risk rather than resolved here.\n\n### Files to Change\n\n| File Path | Change Type | Description |\n|-----------|-------------|-------------|\n| `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh` | Modify | Add the option, its validation, the shared reported-percentage value, the post-output exit gate, and the help/exit-code text |\n| `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/calculate-completeness-script.vitest.ts` | Modify | Cover below/at/above threshold, unchanged report, invalid input, and the `--json` and `--file` paths |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:scope -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:requirements -->\n## 4. REQUIREMENTS\n\n### P0 - Blockers (MUST complete)\n\n| ID | Requirement | Acceptance Criteria |\n|----|-------------|---------------------|\n| REQ-001 | `calculate-completeness.sh` accepts `--min-percent <N>` as an option in any position among the existing options, and leaves the gate inactive when the option is absent. | `bash calculate-completeness.sh --min-percent 50 specs/001-x` parses without a usage error; the same folder without the flag still exits `0` as it does today. |\n| REQ-002 | With `--min-percent <N>`, the script exits `3` when the reported completion percentage is strictly below `N`, and exits `0` when it is at or above `N`. | A packet measured at 40% exits `3` under `--min-percent 50`, exits `0` under `--min-percent 40`, and exits `0` under `--min-percent 30`. |\n| REQ-003 | The report is unchanged: text and `--json` output are byte-identical with and without `--min-percent`. | `diff` of the stdout of the two invocations on the same packet is empty, for both the default and `--json` output modes. |\n\n### P1 - Required (complete OR user-approved deferral)\n\n| ID | Requirement | Acceptance Criteria |\n|----|-------------|---------------------|\n| REQ-004 | A missing, non-integer, or out-of-range `N` is rejected with a message on stderr and exit `1`, and no report is printed. | `--min-percent`, `--min-percent abc`, `--min-percent -1` and `--min-percent 101` each exit `1` with an error naming the option; stdout stays empty. |\n| REQ-005 | The threshold applies to the percentage the run actually reports: `OVERALL_PERCENTAGE` in folder mode and the single file's completion in `--file` mode, with the gate still active under `--json`. | A `--file` run at 0% under `--min-percent 1` exits `3`; the same run under `--json` preserves both the payload and the status. |\n| REQ-006 | `--help` lists `--min-percent <N>` in its OPTIONS block, and the script's trailing exit-code comment documents exit `3`. | `--help` output contains the new option line; the comment block at the end of the file names status `3` and its meaning. |\n| REQ-007 | When `--json` and `--min-percent <N>` are passed together, the JSON output gains a boolean `min_percent_met` field, `true` when the reported completion percentage is at or above `N` and `false` when it is below. | A `--json --min-percent 50` run on a packet at 40% prints `\"min_percent_met\": false` and exits `3`; the same run under `--min-percent 40` prints `\"min_percent_met\": true` and exits `0`. |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:requirements -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n## 5. SUCCESS CRITERIA\n\n- **SC-001**: The three threshold outcomes are observable as distinct exit statuses, verified by script invocation rather than by reading the source.\n- **SC-002**: A byte-for-byte comparison of the report with and without the flag is empty in both output modes.\n- **SC-003**: The existing vitest cases in `calculate-completeness-script.vitest.ts` still pass unchanged, and the new cases cover every row of REQ-001 through REQ-006.\n\n**Acceptance scenarios**\n\n- **Given** a packet whose `Overall Completion` is 40%, **When** the script runs with `--min-percent 50`, **Then** it prints the same report it prints without the flag and exits `3`.\n- **Given** the same packet, **When** the script runs with `--min-percent 40`, **Then** it prints that report and exits `0`, because the floor is inclusive.\n- **Given** any packet, **When** the script runs with no `--min-percent`, **Then** it exits `0` exactly as it did before the change.\n- **Given** a `--min-percent` value that is not an integer from `0` to `100`, **When** the script runs, **Then** it writes a usage error to stderr, prints no report, and exits `1`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:risks -->\n## 6. RISKS & DEPENDENCIES\n\n| Type | Item | Impact | Mitigation |\n|------|------|--------|------------|\n| Dependency | `bc`, plus the `find`/`grep`/`wc` coreutils the script already requires | None beyond today's baseline; the gate adds no new binary | Reuse the existing `command -v bc` guard; no new dependency is introduced |\n| Dependency | `set -euo pipefail` with `trap ... EXIT` | An unset or empty `N` would abort on `$2` under `set -u` with an unhelpful message, and the trap must still clean the temp directory on the new exit path | Read the value as `${2:-}` before use, and exit only after the report is written so the trap runs normally |\n| Risk | Exit `3` collides with the repository's spec-script taxonomy, where `3` means a system error | Medium - a caller that branches on `3` cannot distinguish \"below floor\" from \"I/O failure\" | The feature fixes the status at `3`; the collision is documented in the script's exit-code comment so the meaning stays discoverable |\n| Risk | The gate must not perturb the report | Medium - a stray `echo` or a reordered statement breaks callers that diff output | Gate after both output functions return, and assert byte equality in the test suite |\n| Risk | A caller runs the script under `set -e` and now sees a non-zero status it did not handle | Low - only callers that opt in pass the flag | Opt-in only: with no flag, the status is unchanged |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:risks -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:questions -->\n## 7. OPEN QUESTIONS\n\nNone. The feature statement fixes the option name, its argument, and the two statuses; the remaining choices (validation bounds, the value compared in `--file` mode) are recorded as requirements rather than left open.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:questions -->\n\n---\n","_meta":{"cognition.ai/linesAdded":1,"cognition.ai/linesRemoved":0}}],"locations":[{"path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/wff82223311/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/spec.md"}],"rawInput":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/wff82223311/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/spec.md"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"edit"}}
